   "say": "These six small charts show option payoffs at expiration, per share, with a fifty dollar strike. The long call starts at a loss equal to the premium and gains without limit once the stock passes the strike plus the premium. The short call is the mirror image: the writer keeps the premium at best and faces unlimited loss. The long put gains as the stock falls below the strike minus the premium, with a maximum gain of the strike minus the premium. The short put is its mirror. The covered call caps the upside in exchange for the premium, and the protective put sets a floor while keeping the upside open. Breakeven is the strike plus the premium for calls and the strike minus the premium for puts, the same for buyer and writer. Multiply by one hundred for a contract."
