   "at": "efficient frontier, CML and SML",
   "say": "Last visuals: the efficient frontier, the capital market line, and the security market line. The blue curve is the efficient frontier, the best expected return for each level of total risk. Anything below the bend is inefficient. The red capital market line runs from the risk free rate and just touches the frontier at the market portfolio. It plots total risk, standard deviation, and applies to efficient portfolios. The security market line on the next chart plots beta instead, and it prices every individual security using the CAPM. A stock plotting above the line has positive alpha and looks undervalued; below the line, it looks overvalued. To a client: every portfolio on that top curve gives the most return we can get for its level of swings, and our job is to pick your spot on it."
